<title>USA: TABLE - Bristol-Myers sells century debt.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Bristol-Myers sells century debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Bristol-Myers Squibb Co was priced on Thursday, via lead manager Goldman Sachs &amp; Co, according to a market source.</p>
<p>Bristol-Myers, manufacturers durgs, medical devices infant nutritionals and toiletries.</p>
<p>BORROWER BRISTOL-MYERS SQUIBB CO</p>
<p>AMT $300 MLN	 COUPON 6.875 PCT  MATURITY 8/1/2097</p>
<p>TYPE DEBENTURES    ISS PRICE  99.564 FIRST PAY DATE 2/1/1998</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S AAA   YIELD 6.905 PCT   PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P AAA	 SPREAD +44 BPS    MAKE-WHOLE-CALL AT +15</p>
<p>						  BPS OVER U.S. TREASURIES</p>
<p>((Caryn Trokie, U.S. corporate bond unit, 212-859-1678 ))</p>
